.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Key exchange (RFC 4253 section 8, RFC 5656, RFC 8731 and the hybrid drafts), as computations on byte strings.
.PP
This is the cryptography of a key exchange without its messages: the ephemeral values that go in SSH_MSG_KEX_ECDH_INIT and _REPLY (called KEX_HYBRID_INIT and _REPLY for the hybrid methods; both are messages 30 and 31), the shared secret K, the exchange hash H, and the derivation of keys from them.  conn.h drives the message flow.
.PP
The methods are those of policy.h.  Each has a client value (Q_C, the "init" value) and a server value (Q_S, the "reply" value):
.PP
.nf
.RS
curve25519\-sha256        X25519 public key, 32 bytes
ecdh\-sha2\-nistp256/384   uncompressed point, 65 / 97 bytes
hybrids                  the post\-quantum part first (the KEM public
                         key from the client, the ciphertext from the
                         server), then the classical part
.RE
.fi
.PP
K is an mpint for the plain methods and a string (the hash of the two shared secrets) for the hybrids; gf_kex_secret remembers which.
